  "caveats": "The >=6-discordant floor is a NECESSARY CEILING on per-area power (assumes ALL pairs discordant in one direction); true per-area power is LOWER, so 'can_ever_reject' over-counts resolvable areas. Verified counts are the e-0028 per-area PROJECTION, not a Modal round-trip. Construct = substantive-frontier presence (e-0032); leakage measured clean at target level (e-0049). Super-area coarsening is a reporting aggregation, not a new split. The headline gap x model-SIZE interaction needs MORE power than this single-comparison per-area MDE, so per-area interaction is even less resolvable.",
  "interpretation": "Pooled, the within-deep route's granularity effect is resolvable (n_eff ~115 >> 6). But e-0008's PER-AREA ablation is mostly DEAD. Two filters: (i) the >= 6-discordant combinatorial CEILING is cleared by only 7/17 fine areas; (ii) the sharper filter -- a REACHABLE 80%-power MDE (gap<=0.50) -- is met by only 2/17 (MeasureTheory n_eff=30 MDE~0.28, Analysis n_eff=27 MDE~0.31). The other 5 floor-clearing areas (RingTheory/NumberTheory/LinearAlgebra/Topology/Algebra, n_eff 6-9) can COMBINATORIALLY reject but need a >0.50 gap -- effectively unpowered, the e-0045 trap one notch up. Coarsening into 4 super-areas, only 2/4 are genuinely powered (Analysis* n_eff=70 MDE~0.16-0.20, Algebra* n_eff=34 MDE~0.25-0.30), covering 90% of GB targets; Foundational* clears the count floor (n_eff=6) but its MDE is unreachable. RECOMMENDATION for e-0008: report the granularity gap POOLED (the powered headline), and break it down by AT MOST the 2 genuinely-powered super-areas (Analysis*, Algebra*) -- NOT the 17 fine areas, 15 of which would print an under-powered placeholder. This enforces the e-0045 floor at the ablation granularity Stage 3 actually plans to report, and confirms the per-area interaction (gap x model-SIZE within an area) is out of reach entirely."
